  "content": [
    {
      "text": "thou shalt break his yoke from off thy neck, Gen. 27:40. I have broken the bands of your yoke, Lev. 26:13. he shall put a yoke of iron upon thy neck, Deut. 28:48. Thy father made our yoke grievous, 1 Kgs. 12:4 (2 Chr. 10:4). thou hast broken the yoke of his burden, Isa. 9:4 (2 Ne. 19:4). taken … his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing, Isa. 10:27 (Jer. 30:8; 2 Ne. 20:27). then shall his yoke depart from off them, Isa. 14:25 (2 Ne. 24:25). oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke, Isa. 58:6. broken the yoke, and burst the bonds, Jer. 5:5 (Ezek. 34:27). I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon, Jer. 28:2. took the yoke from off the prophet Jeremiah’s neck, Jer. 28:10. as they that take off the yoke on their jaws, Hosea 11:4. now will I break his yoke from off thee, Nahum 1:13.",
